---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import SiteHeader from '../components/SiteHeader.astro';
import SiteFooter from '../components/SiteFooter.astro';
import EditorialHero from '../components/EditorialHero.astro';

const steps = [
  ['01', 'Send your site details', 'The first step is practical. Share the location, access, planning status, preferred size, budget range, timeline and any drawings, survey material or site photographs.'],
  ['02', 'Feasibility review', 'Bauhu reviews the site conditions, likely route to delivery, model suitability, custom residence potential and any early constraints that may affect scope or cost.'],
  ['03', 'Define the right route', 'Some clients are best served by adapting a Bauhu model. Others require a custom residence shaped more closely around the land, outlook and brief.'],
  ['04', 'Design and engineering', 'Architecture, structure, openings, envelope, foundations strategy, specification and logistics are coordinated against the approved project information.'],
  ['05', 'Controlled procurement and manufacture', 'Approved project information drives the component and procurement package so supplier orders, manufactured elements and project requirements stay aligned before shipment.'],
  ['06', 'Consolidate and ship', 'Bauhu coordinates consolidation and shipping so the building package is organised against the approved project information before dispatch. Containerisation, handling and the realities of the destination are considered as part of delivery.'],
  ['07', 'Assembly guidance and support', 'The local team receives project-specific assembly information covering sequencing, connections and key construction stages. Bauhu remains available during assembly to assist with technical questions and interpretation of the project information.'],
];
---
<BaseLayout title="How It Works | Bauhu" description="The guided Bauhu buyer journey from site review to design, manufacture and delivery.">
  <SiteHeader />
  <main>
    <EditorialHero
      eyebrow="Guided buyer journey"
      title="A clear route from land to residence."
      text="Bauhu helps clients understand what is possible before committing to a full design and manufacturing process. The journey begins with the realities of the site."
      primaryHref="/site-fit"
      primaryLabel="Start your project"
      imageSrc="/images/developments/bauhu-how-it-works-hero.webp"
    />
    <section class="section-pad bg-paper">
      <div class="mx-auto grid max-w-site gap-12 lg:grid-cols-[0.85fr_1.15fr]">
        <div>
          <p class="eyebrow text-clay">Process</p>
          <h2 class="mt-5 font-display text-4xl leading-tight md:text-6xl">Designed to reduce uncertainty before you commit.</h2>
        </div>
        <p class="text-lg leading-8 text-ink/70">Remote, coastal and island projects need clarity early. Bauhu’s process is designed to identify the right route, the likely constraints and the practical delivery path before detailed work begins.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="mx-auto mt-14 grid max-w-site gap-5 md:grid-cols-2">
        {steps.map(([number, title, text]) => (
          <article class="bg-mist p-7 md:p-10">
            <p class="text-sm text-clay">{number}</p>
            <h2 class="mt-10 font-display text-4xl">{title}</h2>
            <p class="mt-5 leading-7 text-ink/70">{text}</p>
          </article>
        ))}
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section-pad bg-ink text-paper">
      <div class="mx-auto grid max-w-site gap-12 lg:grid-cols-[0.9fr_1.1fr]">
        <div>
          <p class="eyebrow text-stone">Controlled delivery</p>
          <h2 class="mt-5 font-display text-4xl leading-tight md:text-6xl">Designed to be built, shipped and assembled — not simply designed to be drawn.</h2>
        </div>
        <div class="space-y-6 text-lg leading-8 text-paper/70">
          <p>Remote construction becomes expensive when design changes, procurement mistakes, labour shortages and repeat shipments are discovered on site. Bauhu moves more decisions upstream, where they can be coordinated before the building reaches the site.</p>
          <p>That means one controlled flow of approved design information into engineering, procurement, manufacture, consolidation and shipping — with a clear record of what belongs in the Bauhu package and what remains a local responsibility.</p>
          <p>Delivery is not the end of Bauhu’s involvement. Project-specific assembly information is issued to support the local contractor, and the Bauhu team remains available during assembly to assist with technical questions and interpretation of the coordinated project information.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="mx-auto mt-12 grid max-w-site gap-5 md:grid-cols-3">
        {['Approved project information','Consolidation / shipping control','Assembly guide / technical support'].map((label) => (
          <div class="flex min-h-64 items-center justify-center border border-paper/15 p-6 text-center">
            <div><p class="eyebrow text-stone">IMAGE PLACEHOLDER</p><p class="mt-4 text-sm text-paper/55">{label}</p></div>
          </div>
        ))}
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section-pad bg-mist">
      <div class="mx-auto grid max-w-site gap-12 lg:grid-cols-[0.9fr_1.1fr]">
        <div>
          <p class="eyebrow text-clay">Logistics & assembly support</p>
          <h2 class="mt-5 font-display text-4xl leading-tight md:text-6xl">One coordinated shipment. Support that continues after delivery.</h2>
        </div>
        <div class="space-y-6 text-lg leading-8 text-ink/70">
          <p>Bauhu coordinates procurement, consolidation and shipping as connected parts of the building delivery process. Components are brought together against the approved project information before dispatch so the shipment is treated as one coordinated building package rather than a collection of unrelated supplier deliveries.</p>
          <p>For assembly, Bauhu provides detailed project information covering structural sequencing, connections, envelope installation, material requirements and key construction stages. The information is designed to aid the local contractor and installers; it does not replace the responsibilities or professional judgement of the appointed site team.</p>
          <p>During assembly, Bauhu remains available to assist with technical questions and interpretation of the project documentation.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section-pad bg-paper">
      <div class="mx-auto max-w-site">
        <p class="eyebrow text-clay">After you enquire</p>
        <h2 class="mt-5 max-w-4xl font-display text-4xl leading-tight md:text-6xl">A serious first review, not a generic sales callback.</h2>
        <div class="mt-12 grid gap-5 md:grid-cols-3">
          <article class="bg-mist p-7"><h3 class="font-display text-3xl">We review the site</h3><p class="mt-4 leading-7 text-ink/70">Location, access, exposure, planning position and any survey or drawings you already have.</p></article>
          <article class="bg-mist p-7"><h3 class="font-display text-3xl">We identify the route</h3><p class="mt-4 leading-7 text-ink/70">Predesigned model, custom design or larger development — and the main constraints that should be resolved first.</p></article>
          <article class="bg-mist p-7"><h3 class="font-display text-3xl">We define the next decision</h3><p class="mt-4 leading-7 text-ink/70">The objective is clarity on feasibility, scope and what information is needed before meaningful design or pricing work proceeds.</p></article>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>
  <SiteFooter />
</BaseLayout>
